    "disfavor": {
      "word": "DISFAVOR",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "Want of favor of favorable regard; disesteem; disregard. The people that deserved my disfavor. Is. x. 6 (1551). Sentiment of disfavor against its ally. Gladstone.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "The state of not being in favor; a being under the displeasure of some one; state of unacceptableness; as, to be in disfavor at court.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "An unkindness; a disobliging act. He might dispense favors and disfavors. Clarendon.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "To withhold or withdraw favor from; to regard with disesteem; to show disapprobation of; to discountenance. Countenanced or disfavored according as they obey. Swift.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To injure the form or looks of. [R.] B. Jonson.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        }
      ],
